The lines you’ve provided are from **Shakespeare’s Sonnet 2**, one of the 1609 sonnets attributed to William Shakespeare. This particular sonnet is part of the “Fair Youth” sequence — the first several sonnets addressed to a young man, encouraging him to procreate and preserve his beauty for future generations.

### Here's Sonnet 2 in full:

> When I do count the clock that tells the time,  
> And see the brave day sunk in hideous night;  
> When I behold the violet past prime,  
> And sable curls all silver'd o'er with white;
